course: dictionary
lesson: 11724
title: Helping words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Auxiliary means giving extra help or support. An auxiliary engine is a backup that helps when the main engine is not enough. In grammar, an auxiliary is a helping verb that works with another verb, like «She is running» or «I have eaten».
explain: The helping verbs be, have and do are the most common auxiliaries. Look at «She is running»: is helps running, so is is the auxiliary. In «I have eaten», have helps eaten. Find the main verb first, then look for the small word just before it.
explain: Modal verbs such as can, will and must are auxiliaries too. In «He will come tomorrow», will is the auxiliary, and it shows that the coming is in the future. Modal verbs never change their form, so you cannot say «he cans».
fact: Auxiliary means giving extra help or support.
fact: An auxiliary verb is a helping verb, like be, have or do, used with another verb.
fact: «She is running» and «I have eaten» both use an auxiliary verb to help the main verb.
fact: Modal verbs like can, will and must are also auxiliaries: «She can swim».
fact: An auxiliary can also be a helper or extra worker, like a nursing auxiliary who supports the nurses.
exercise: «They have finished their lunch.» Which word is the auxiliary verb? | *have | lunch | They | finished
exercise: What does auxiliary mean in «an auxiliary engine»? | A broken engine | *A backup that gives extra help | A small toy engine | A very loud engine
exercise: «She can swim.» Which word is a modal auxiliary? | Nothing | She | *can | swim
test: What is a nursing auxiliary? | A machine that checks heartbeats | A type of medicine given to patients | A kind of nurse's uniform | *A helper or extra worker who supports the nurses
test: In «Did you see the film?», which word is the auxiliary? | see | you | *Did | film
exam: Which word in «The dog was barking» is an auxiliary verb? | dog | The | *was | barking
